WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.456
You recorded Exposure Management as
not applicable in a government cloud,

3
00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:07.525
and used the interim path instead.

4
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:10.534
You filed the vulnerability
and exposure queries,

5
00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:14.187
and checked that each exposed
device has an owner and a ticket.

6
00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:16.395
And you exported the open incidents,

7
00:00:16.395 --> 00:00:19.263
and one incident with its
alerts, for the record.

8
00:00:19.263 --> 00:00:22.064
The evidence an I S S O
keeps from this module:

9
00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:25.878
the vulnerability query output
and the remediation queue;

10
00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:29.770
the severity table and the
incident response plan's version;

11
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.517
the monthly incident export, with
alerts, classification and timestamps;

12
00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:38.487
and every incident closed outside
its window, with the reason.

13
00:00:38.487 --> 00:00:45.000
Next is Module 4: hunting, detections as
code, and identity and cloud-app signals.
